course: dictionary
lesson: 7273
title: One word, two jobs: pinball
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pinball is a game played on a machine. A metal ball shoots up a sloping table, and you use flippers to hit it so it keeps bouncing off targets and you score points.
explain: Pinball can also be a verb, which means to bounce quickly from one place to another. «The ball pinballed around the box.» The ball did not stay still. It bounced from side to side, again and again.
explain: Read the example carefully: «Jupiter's huge gravity acts like a pinball flipper for comets and asteroids.» Jupiter is not a machine. The word pinball is used to compare Jupiter's pull to a machine's flipper, which sends things away or towards other places.
fact: A pinball machine has a sloping table, a metal ball, and flippers.
fact: Pinball machines are found in arcades and cafes, and the game can also be played on computers.
fact: «Pinballed» is an informal verb meaning to bounce quickly from one place to another.
fact: A flipper, in pinball, is a moving part that knocks the ball back into play.
fact: When one thing is said to act «like a pinball flipper», the words compare two things to show how they work.
exercise: What do you use to keep the ball bouncing in pinball? | Sails | Ropes | *Flippers | Wheels
exercise: «The ball pinballed around the box.» What does pinballed mean? | To paint something bright | To sleep quietly in one spot | *To bounce quickly from one place to another | To fall straight down
exercise: In «Jupiter's gravity acts like a pinball flipper», what is the gravity being compared to? | A library book | *A pinball flipper | A cup of tea | A football goal
test: Which word in «The ball pinballed around the box» shows the ball moved quickly from place to place? | Box | Ball | *Pinballed | Around
test: What is pinball when it is a game? | A kind of ball you kick on a pitch | *An arcade game with a metal ball on a sloping table | A type of quiet, slow board game | A machine that makes ice cream
exam: In the sentence «Jupiter's gravity acts like a pinball flipper for comets», what does the comparison tell you about how Jupiter's gravity affects comets? | It turns them into ice | *It can knock them away or send them towards other places, like a flipper hitting a ball | It makes them glow like lamps | It makes them stop moving completely
